#: ../../../explanation/what-is-the-menu-key.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn what the Menu key on your keyboard does in Ubuntu Desktop, how it "
"opens context menus, and what to use if your keyboard lacks one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/what-is-the-menu-key.md:7
msgid "Topics: Keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/what-is-the-menu-key.md:11
msgid "What is the Menu key?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/what-is-the-menu-key.md:13
msgid ""
"The {kbd}`Menu` key, also known as the *Application* key, is a key found on "
"some Windows-oriented keyboards. This key is usually on the bottom-right of "
"the keyboard, next to the {kbd}`Ctrl` key, but it can be placed in a "
"different location by keyboard manufacturers. It is usually depicted as a "
"cursor hovering above a menu: {kbd}`≣🡴`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/what-is-the-menu-key.md:15
msgid ""
"The primary function of this key is to launch a context menu with the "
"keyboard rather than by clicking the right mouse button: this is useful if "
"mouse or a similar device is not available, or when the right mouse button "
"is not present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/what-is-the-menu-key.md:17
msgid ""
"The {kbd}`Menu` key is sometimes omitted in the interest of space, "
"particularly on portable and laptop keyboards. In this case, some keyboards "
"include a {kbd}`Menu` function key that can be activated in combination with "
"the Function ({kbd}`Fn`) key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/what-is-the-menu-key.md:19
msgid ""
"The *context menu* is a menu that pops up when you right-click. The menu "
"that you see, if any, is dependent on the context and function of the area "
"that you right-clicked. When you use the {kbd}`Menu` key, the context menu "
"is shown for the area of the screen that your cursor is over at the point "
"when the key is pressed."
msgstr ""
